cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use MutCert in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "MutCert: Transparent, Parameter-Free Protein Stability Change Estimation"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-06-02
authors:
  - family-names: Towfigh
    given-names: Nasser
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/nassertowfigh/mutcert"
keywords:
  - protein stability
  - mutation effect prediction
  - glass-box machine learning
  - Miyazawa-Jernigan potential
  - convergence certification
  - BFS energy propagation
abstract: >
  MutCert is a transparent, parameter-free BFS energy estimator for
  protein stability change (ΔΔG) prediction. It achieves Spearman |ρ|
  0.449 on T4 lysozyme (comparable to DDGun-seq on the same S2648 val
  split) using zero force-field tuning. Its distinguishing contribution
  is auditability: every per-step energy attribution is recorded via
  glass-box BFS trace, enabling full inspection of how each residue
  contributes to the final prediction.
